---
title: "valid - transaction_validity_check (Sui Whitepaper: Owners and Authorization)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_iter_inputs: for each input object in inputs(Tx)
    q_iter_inputs --> q_classify: classify object type
    q_classify --> q_check_readonly: read-only object
    q_classify --> q_check_owned: owned object
    q_classify --> q_check_shared: shared object

    q_check_readonly --> q_readonly_pass: authorized (no owner check needed)
    q_readonly_pass --> q_next_input: object authorized

    q_check_owned --> q_check_owner_type: inspect owner(Obj)
    q_check_owner_type --> q_check_addr_sig: owner is address
    q_check_owner_type --> q_check_parent_input: owner is ObjID (child object)

    q_check_addr_sig --> q_addr_pass: Tx signed by owner address
    q_check_addr_sig --> q_addr_fail: Tx not signed by owner address
    q_addr_pass --> q_check_mutability: verify mutability permissions match
    q_addr_fail --> q_invalid: return false

    q_check_parent_input --> q_parent_pass: parent object included in Tx inputs and authorized
    q_check_parent_input --> q_parent_fail: parent object not in inputs
    q_parent_pass --> q_check_mutability
    q_parent_fail --> q_invalid

    q_check_mutability --> q_next_input: permissions match (Obj, mut Obj, or immut Obj)
    q_check_mutability --> q_invalid: permissions mismatch

    q_check_shared --> q_shared_pass: shared objects perform own authorization logic
    q_shared_pass --> q_next_input

    q_next_input --> q_iter_inputs: more inputs remaining
    q_next_input --> q_valid: all inputs authorized
    q_valid --> [*]: return true
    q_invalid --> [*]: return false

    note right of q_check_owner_type
        INV-001: Single transaction can use objects owned by only one address
        INV-002: Child objects require parent object in transaction inputs
        INV-003: Read-only objects usable by any transaction without authorization
        INV-004: Shared mutable objects require consensus for version assignment
    end note
